  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 334511) has recorded $13.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Contracting activity includes 8,066 awards with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations fell 28.7% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows previous totals of $13.2B in FY21, $13.9B in FY22, $17B in FY23, $16.8B in FY24, and $18.4B in FY25. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $10.8B in obligations, followed by the Department of Transportation with $1.1B and the Department of Homeland Security with $943M. RAYTHEON COMPANY, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, and NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION appear among the largest vendors, with multiple entries across the top-ten vendor list. This profile highlights a concentrated buyer base and a small set of large suppliers driving most obligations in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the current spending level and recent trend for NAICS 334511?",
